# Words and paths codespell gets wrong here, and why.
#
# Same rule as every other ignore list in this repository: an entry names the
# condition that would remove it, so the file stays a set of decisions rather
# than an accumulation nobody can audit. See the de-bloat driver in
# docs/epochs/02-abstraction.md.
#
#   iif  - iproute2's "incoming interface" selector, as in
#          `ip route get <addr> from <src> iif <iface>`. codespell reads it as
#          a misspelling of "if". It is the flag's real name, it appears in the
#          epoch record because that command is what diagnosed the VRF routing
#          fault, and it will appear again in any nftables or policy-routing
#          note. Removed when: never.
#
# The skip list below was Super-Linter's FILTER_REGEX_EXCLUDE until #365 took
# that aggregate out. It lives here now for the reason the split was made at
# all - one owner per check - and because a path exclusion kept in the CI
# configuration behaves differently from one kept here: codespell run by hand
# would not honour it, so a clean local run stopped predicting a clean lane.
#
# clusters/management/flux-system/ is Flux's own generated install and sync
# manifest, committed verbatim so it goes through normal review like everything
# else. It is not ours to edit, so a finding inside it is a finding about
# Flux's upstream manifest rather than about this codebase; codespell objects
# to a hyphenated form of "reuse" in one of its comments. Structural validity
# is still checked by the Validate lane's kubeconform pass, which this does not
# affect. Removed when: the manifest stops being vendored verbatim.
#
# clusters/bootstrap/ is Cilium's chart output, committed verbatim - the same
# case, excluded for the same reason. codespell objects to one of Kubernetes'
# CamelCase label-selector operators inside it, reading it as a misspelling of
# two ordinary words; it is the operator's real name, and nothing edits that
# file by hand since `task render-cni` regenerates it. Removed when: the
# rendered output stops being committed.
#
# pnpm-lock.yaml and go.sum are generated integrity databases: long runs of
# base64 and hex, inside which codespell reliably finds "misspellings". Nothing
# edits either by hand and no linter here has anything useful to say about
# them. Removed when: never, while they are generated.
#
# ./coverage is the test suites' own HTML report, gitignored and so invisible to
# the CI lane but not to a local run - which is the divergence this file exists
# to remove. The prettified JavaScript bundled into that report contains a
# contraction written without its apostrophe. Removed when: the report stops
# being generated into the working tree.
#
# The flagged fragments are described rather than quoted on purpose. An earlier
# version of this note spelled two of them out literally and codespell promptly
# flagged the comment instead of the file it was excluding.
[codespell]
ignore-words-list = iif
skip = ./.git,./coverage,./node_modules,./clusters/management/flux-system,./clusters/bootstrap,./pnpm-lock.yaml,*/go.sum,*/node_modules
